# johnhringiv.com deploy config — copy to a private env file next to the
# scripts (e.g. `johnhringiv.env`), fill it in, and `chmod 600` it.
#
# The production host runs TWO app containers behind HAProxy (on pfSense): a
# primary and a backup. HAProxy serves the primary and fails over to the
# backup when the primary's /nginx-health check stops answering. deploy.sh
# recreates them one at a time — backup first, then primary — health-gating
# each before moving on, so at least one instance is always serving. That is
# the zero-downtime story.

# Image to run. Continuous deploy pulls the :prod tag that the Deploy workflow
# promotes; pin a sha-… tag to roll back, or point at :latest to ship every
# push to main without pressing the Deploy button.
IMAGE=ghcr.io/johnhringiv/johnhringiv.com:prod

# Container names — must match the servers HAProxy's backends point at.
CONTAINER_PRIMARY=johnhringiv-primary
CONTAINER_BACKUP=johnhringiv-backup

# Host ports each container publishes (the container listens on 8080 inside).
# HAProxy's primary/backup backends target these host ports.
PORT_PRIMARY=8080
PORT_BACKUP=8081

# Local health endpoint (nginx returns 200 "healthy"; see config/nginx.conf).
# deploy.sh gates each container on this before touching the next.
HEALTH_PATH=/nginx-health

# Public URL for the poller's edge check (through Cloudflare). Optional but
# recommended — lets poll-deploy.sh flag when the site is down at the edge even
# though the containers look healthy locally (Cloudflare/HAProxy/DNS trouble).
PUBLIC_URL=https://johnhringiv.com
